# -----------------------------
# Engineering source firewall
# -----------------------------
# Real engineering documentation is an EXTERNAL input to this project. It is
# client material: drawings, cable schedules and their exports never belong in
# version control, regardless of which directory they are dropped into.
#
# `storage/` above already excludes the runtime document store. These rules are
# defence in depth for the case that actually happened once: a source drawing
# added from another path, or forced past an ignore rule. The repository ships
# no PDF, workbook or CAD asset of its own, so a blanket rule costs nothing.
#
# If a genuinely public documentation asset is ever needed, add it with an
# explicit negation (`!docs/assets/example.pdf`) and say why in the commit.
*.pdf
*.xlsx
*.xlsm
*.xls
*.dwg
*.dxf
*.dwf
*.step
*.stp
*.iges

# Scans and exported drawing images
*.tif
*.tiff

# Extraction and pipeline outputs derived from source documents
knowledge/extraction/outputs/**/*
!knowledge/extraction/outputs/**/README.md

# -----------------------------
# Local databases and dumps
# -----------------------------
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db-journal
*.sql.gz
*.dump

